sequenceDiagram
    %% ShiftManager Dual Authentication Flow
    %% Shows both Standard Login and Griffin ADFS (SAML SSO)

    participant User as 👤 User Browser
    participant LoginPage as 📄 /Auth/Login
    participant RateLimiter as ⏱️ RateLimitingService
    participant PasswordHasher as 🔐 PasswordHasher (PBKDF2)
    participant Griffin as 🏢 Griffin ADFS
    participant GriffinService as 🔧 GriffinService
    participant DB as 💿 SQLite Database
    participant AuthMiddleware as ⚙️ ASP.NET Auth
    participant HomePage as 🏠 /Home/Index

    %% ========================================
    %% STANDARD LOGIN FLOW (Email/Password)
    %% ========================================

    Note over User,HomePage: Standard Login Flow (Email/Password)

    User->>LoginPage: Navigate to /Auth/Login
    LoginPage-->>User: Show login form

    User->>LoginPage: Submit (Email, Password)

    LoginPage->>RateLimiter: Check rate limit (login:{IP})
    alt Rate limit exceeded (10 attempts / 15 min)
        RateLimiter-->>LoginPage: Rejected
        LoginPage-->>User: Error: "Rate limit exceeded"
    end

    LoginPage->>LoginPage: Validate input:<br/>• Required fields<br/>• Email format (regex)<br/>• Max length (Email: 255, Password: 500)

    LoginPage->>DB: Query user by Email<br/>WHERE Email = @Email AND IsActive = true<br/>(IgnoreQueryFilters for multi-tenancy)
    DB-->>LoginPage: AppUser or null

    alt User not found or inactive
        LoginPage->>LoginPage: Log: "User not found"
        LoginPage-->>User: Error: "Invalid credentials"<br/>(Generic message)
    end

    alt Account locked out
        LoginPage->>LoginPage: Check: LockoutEnd > NOW
        LoginPage-->>User: Error: "Account locked for {X} minutes"
    end

    LoginPage->>PasswordHasher: Verify(password, user.PasswordHash, user.PasswordSalt)

    Note over PasswordHasher: PBKDF2 Hash Verification:<br/>• 100,000 iterations<br/>• SHA-256<br/>• Fixed-time comparison

    PasswordHasher-->>LoginPage: bool (true/false)

    alt Password incorrect
        LoginPage->>DB: UPDATE Users SET<br/>FailedLoginAttempts++,<br/>LastLoginAttempt = NOW
        alt FailedLoginAttempts >= 10
            LoginPage->>DB: UPDATE Users SET<br/>LockoutEnd = NOW + 30 minutes
            LoginPage-->>User: Error: "Account locked after 10 attempts"
        else
            LoginPage-->>User: Error: "Invalid credentials"<br/>(Attempt {X}/10)
        end
    end

    LoginPage->>DB: Reset failed attempts:<br/>FailedLoginAttempts = 0,<br/>LockoutEnd = NULL
    LoginPage->>RateLimiter: Reset rate limit (login:{IP})

    LoginPage->>LoginPage: Create Claims:<br/>• NameIdentifier (UserId)<br/>• Name (DisplayName)<br/>• Role (Manager, Owner, etc.)<br/>• CompanyId (for multi-tenancy)

    LoginPage->>AuthMiddleware: SignInAsync(ClaimsPrincipal)

    Note over AuthMiddleware: Create Cookie:<br/>.AspNetCore.Cookies<br/>• 7-day sliding expiration<br/>• HttpOnly<br/>• SameSite=Strict<br/>• Secure (in production)

    AuthMiddleware-->>LoginPage: Cookie set
    LoginPage-->>User: Redirect to /Home/Index

    User->>HomePage: Navigate to /Home/Index (with cookie)
    HomePage->>AuthMiddleware: Validate cookie
    AuthMiddleware-->>HomePage: User authenticated (CompanyId=2, Role=Manager)
    HomePage-->>User: Show dashboard

    %% ========================================
    %% GRIFFIN ADFS FLOW (SAML SSO)
    %% ========================================

    Note over User,HomePage: Griffin ADFS Flow (SAML SSO)

    User->>LoginPage: Click "Login with Griffin ADFS"
    LoginPage->>DB: Load GriffinConfig<br/>(BaseUrl, AutoProvisionUsers, etc.)
    alt Griffin not configured or disabled
        LoginPage-->>User: Error: "ADFS not configured"
    end

    LoginPage->>LoginPage: Build authentication URL:<br/>https://griffin.example.com/authentication<br/>?tokenConsumerURL=<double-encoded-callback>

    LoginPage-->>User: Redirect to Griffin ADFS

    User->>Griffin: Navigate to Griffin ADFS
    Griffin-->>User: Show Active Directory login

    User->>Griffin: Enter AD credentials
    Griffin->>Griffin: Validate against Active Directory
    Griffin-->>User: Redirect to callback:<br/>https://app.example.com/Auth/GriffinCallback<br/>?token=abc123xyz

    User->>GriffinService: /Auth/GriffinCallback?token=abc123xyz

    GriffinService->>GriffinService: Check claims cache:<br/>SHA256(token) → 8-hour TTL

    alt Claims cached
        GriffinService->>GriffinService: Use cached claims
    else Cache miss
        GriffinService->>Griffin: GET /authorization/validate?token=abc123xyz
        Griffin-->>GriffinService: "true" or "false"

        alt Token invalid
            GriffinService-->>User: Error: "Invalid token"
        end

        GriffinService->>Griffin: GET /authorization/getClaims?token=abc123xyz
        Griffin-->>GriffinService: GriffinClaimsDto:<br/>{<br/>  UPN: "john.doe@company.com",<br/>  sAMAccountName: "jdoe",<br/>  DisplayName: "John Doe",<br/>  GivenName: "John",<br/>  Surname: "Doe",<br/>  auth_time: "2025-06-15T10:30:00Z"<br/>}

        GriffinService->>GriffinService: Cache claims (8-hour TTL)
    end

    GriffinService->>DB: Query user by UPN (email):<br/>WHERE Email = @UPN AND IsActive = true<br/>(IgnoreQueryFilters for multi-tenancy)
    DB-->>GriffinService: AppUser or null

    alt User not found
        alt AutoProvisionUsers = true
            GriffinService->>DB: INSERT INTO Users:<br/>Email = UPN,<br/>DisplayName = Griffin.DisplayName,<br/>Role = DefaultProvisionedRole,<br/>PasswordHash = empty,<br/>PasswordSalt = empty
            DB-->>GriffinService: New user created (UserId=42)
            GriffinService->>DB: INSERT INTO AuditLogs:<br/>Action = "GriffinAutoProvision"
        else AutoProvisionUsers = false
            GriffinService-->>User: Error: "User not found.<br/>Contact admin for approval."
        end
    end

    GriffinService->>GriffinService: Create Claims:<br/>• NameIdentifier (UserId)<br/>• Name (DisplayName)<br/>• Email (UPN)<br/>• Role (Manager, Employee, etc.)<br/>• CompanyId<br/>• AuthMethod = "Griffin"<br/>• Griffin:sAMAccountName<br/>• Griffin:Token<br/>• Griffin:AuthTime<br/>• AuthTimestamp

    GriffinService->>AuthMiddleware: Set context.User (ClaimsPrincipal)
    GriffinService->>GriffinService: Set cookies:<br/>1. .AspNetCore.Cookies (session)<br/>2. griffin.token (for middleware)

    GriffinService-->>User: Redirect to /Home/Index

    User->>HomePage: Navigate to /Home/Index (with cookies)
    HomePage->>AuthMiddleware: Validate cookies
    AuthMiddleware-->>HomePage: User authenticated (CompanyId=2, AuthMethod=Griffin)
    HomePage-->>User: Show dashboard

    %% ========================================
    %% GRIFFIN MIDDLEWARE RE-VALIDATION
    %% ========================================

    Note over User,HomePage: Subsequent Request (Griffin user)

    User->>HomePage: Navigate to /Schedule
    HomePage->>AuthMiddleware: GriffinAuthenticationMiddleware runs BEFORE UseAuthentication
    AuthMiddleware->>AuthMiddleware: Extract griffin.token cookie
    alt Token present
        AuthMiddleware->>GriffinService: AuthenticateUserAsync(token)
        GriffinService->>GriffinService: Check cache (SHA256 hash)
        alt Claims cached
            GriffinService-->>AuthMiddleware: ClaimsPrincipal (from cache)
        else Cache miss or expired
            GriffinService->>Griffin: Validate token + fetch claims
            Griffin-->>GriffinService: Claims or invalid
            alt Token invalid
                AuthMiddleware->>AuthMiddleware: Delete griffin.token cookie
                AuthMiddleware-->>User: Redirect to /Auth/Login
            else Token valid
                GriffinService-->>AuthMiddleware: ClaimsPrincipal
            end
        end
        AuthMiddleware->>AuthMiddleware: Set context.User = principal
    end
    AuthMiddleware->>HomePage: Continue pipeline
    HomePage-->>User: Show schedule

    %% ========================================
    %% SECURITY SUMMARY
    %% ========================================

    Note over User,HomePage: 🛡️ SECURITY FEATURES:<br/>✓ PBKDF2 password hashing (100K iterations, SHA-256)<br/>✓ Account lockout (10 failed attempts = 30 min)<br/>✓ Rate limiting (10 attempts / 15 min per IP)<br/>✓ Fixed-time password comparison (timing attack prevention)<br/>✓ Cookie security (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Strict)<br/>✓ Griffin token validation + 8-hour cache<br/>✓ Auto-provisioning (optional)<br/>✓ Audit logging (all auth events)
